<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mentēsānus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to the city
			of</i> Mentesa (Mentissa, <i><span class="en">Liv. 26, 17</span></i>) <i>in</i> Hispania Baetica: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ordo Mentesanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 384, 2</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mentesani Bastuli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 3, 4, § 25</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Mentesani Oretani in Hispaniā Tarraconensi, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3,
				4, § 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 26,
			17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
